        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "Page 3",
        "page": 3,
        "text": "The Business may be closed some days over the Christmas and New Year period as\ndetermined by the directors. You will be required to reserve holiday from your entitlement\nto cover this period. The Operations Director will advise you of these and any other closed\ndays applicable each year. For full details for the how to request holidays please refer to your\nEmployee Handbook.\nIf you leave our employment for whatever reason any holiday accrued but not taken will be\npaid with your final monies. Your manager may require you to take any outstanding accrued\nholiday as part of your notice period, a decision on this will be communicated to you with no\nless than five working days’ notice. Any holiday taken but not accrued will be deducted from\nyour final monies.\nABSENCE FROM WORK\nAll sickness absence must be certificated. For absences up to seven days a self-certification\nform must be completed on your return to work and endorsed by a manager. Periods of\nsickness absence in excess of seven days must be supported by a Fitness to Work certificate\navailable through your GP surgery. Your Fitness to Work certificate should be sent to your\nmanager if your absence is for any period in excess of one week. Full details of the absence\nreporting procedures are outlined in your Employee Handbook.\nOn the first day of any sickness absence you must ensure that your manager is informed by\ntelephone of your sickness at the earliest possible opportunity. You should also give details\nof the nature of your illness and the day on which you expect to return to work. You must\ninform the Company as soon as possible of any change in the date of your anticipated return\nto work.\nSTATUTORY SICK PAY (SSP)\nSubject to the eligibility criteria established by HMRC, we pay Statutory Sick Pay for the\ndays you would normally work. (If you work varying days, then your qualifying days are the\ndays you are rostered to work.)\nMEDICALS\nWe reserve the right to arrange an examination by the Company Doctor/Occupational Health\nPractitioner at our expense to establish the nature and extent of any sickness and we may\nalso request your permission to obtain a medical report from your own doctor.\nPROBATIONARY PERIOD\nThe first three months of your employment are covered by a probationary period, when the\ndisciplinary procedures may not apply. Your contract of employment may be ended at any\ntime during this period if you are failing to achieve the necessary standards of performance\nand/or conduct for the successful achievement of your role. At the end of your probationary\nperiod your performance will be assessed and provided you have reached the criteria\nnecessary for the fulfilment of the objectives of your role your position will be confirmed.\nAlternatively, your contract of employment maybe terminated, or the probationary period\nextended for up to a further three months.\n3",
