        "heading": "Page 5",
        "page": 5,
        "text": "The Company wish to encourage and support the staff in their ongoing training and\ndevelopment and will cover the cost of any mandatory training required by the business. In\nthe case of other industry specific training the company may contribute on a case-by-case\nbasis as agreed with the Operations Director. Repayment of the company's contribution\nwill however be required to be repaid should you fail to successfully complete the training or\nchoose to leave the company within one year of completing the training. Repayment will be\napplied on a sliding scale as follows: Failure to successfully complete the training or leaving\nwithin 0 - 12 months 100% of costs to be repaid; leaving within 12-18 months, 50% of costs\nand over 24 months 0% of the costs. Any outstanding costs will be deducted from your\nmonthly salary over a maximum of six months or your final salary.\nFAMILY FRIENDLY POLICIES\nThe Company has in place a number of policies to support those employees responsible for\nthe care of dependants. These include policies relating to Maternity Leave and Pay,\nAntenatal Care, Paternity Leave and Pay, Adoption Leave and Pay, Parental Bereavement\nLeave and Pay, Shared Parental Leave and Pay, Unpaid Parental Leave, Unpaid Time off for\ndomestic emergencies, Compassionate Leave, and Flexible working. Full details of these,\nincluding any statutory eligibility requirements or conditions and the Company's rules\napplicable to each type of leave are contained in your Employee Handbook and are available\nfrom the HR Department.\nHEALTH AND SAFETY\nUnder the Health and Safety at Work Act we all have a legal responsibility to ensure we\nmaintain a safe working environment and comply with all company rules and procedures\nrelating to Health and Safety and to report any potential risks to the Health and Safety of\nourselves or others.\nSTANDARDS OF WORK\nThe Company expects the highest standards of professional behaviour in relation to the\nEmployee’s activities undertaken at work. Failure to adhere to these standards will be\nbrought to the attention of the Employee’s manager. If appropriate, training will be provided,\nbut continual failure to meet these standards could result in action being taken under the\nCompany’s disciplinary or capability procedures. Full details of these are contained in the\nEmployee Handbook.\nMEDIA CONTACT\nYou are not authorised to speak to or contact any branch of the media with regard to any\nmatter affecting the Company, its customers, business associates or other employees without\nprior, written approval of a Director of the Company. If you contact the press or media\nwithout prior consent, the Company may consider this as gross misconduct, which could,\nfollowing proper investigation, lead to your summary dismissal.\nSOCIAL MEDIA\nIf the Company requires you to actively contribute to the content and activity of our social\nmedia accounts such as Facebook, and Instagram you will be expressly advised of this\nresponsibility. In these circumstances, you are expected to represent and reflect the views of\n5",
