    "sectionId": "para-649",
    "filename": "Rockwater Group Employee Handbook (April 2026).docx",
    "context": "[para-645] There will be no further stage of appeal. The decision on the grievance will be final.\n\n[para-647] Simultaneous grievance and disciplinary matters\n\n[para-649] The Organisation will make a decision on how to progress matters when an employee raises a grievance about a disciplinary procedure involving them. ACAS guidance suggests that disciplinary hearings may be suspended for a short duration while the grievance is investigated. The Organisation will assess the exact nature of the grievance and will have the final say over suspension of a disciplinary procedure.\n\n[para-651] Extending timescales under the procedure\n\n[para-653] The timescales outlined in this procedure will be adhered to whenever this is reasonably practicable. There may be extenuating circumstances that are outside of either parties’ control, for example, where a key witness is unavailable or the grievance requires extensive investigation.",
