    "title": "Offering Complimentary Drinks, Food and Services",
    "sectionId": "para-1439",
    "filename": "Rockwater Group Employee Handbook (April 2026).docx",
    "context": "[para-1436] You are responsible for completing all end of day reporting, for the safe keeping of the Company’s monies and stock and the securing of the Company’s premises in accordance with the training you receive relating to cash and stock handling and security of the building.\n\n[para-1438] Offering Complimentary Drinks, Food and Services\n\n[para-1439] Complimentary drinks and food may be offered by senior managers and directors in order to promote the business. No other member of the team is authorised to offer complimentary drinks, food or services.\n\n[para-1441] The offering of complimentary drinks, food or services should not be used for personal gain, such as receiving reciprocal benefits from another business. Abuse of this rule is considered to amount to an act of Gross Misconduct and may, following proper investigation lead to summary dismissal.\n\n[para-1443] Health and safety",
    "note": "Original DOCX paragraph anchors count blank paragraphs and are not page numbers. This is documentary wording, not a finding about the incident. The supplied handbook contains template placeholders elsewhere; where relevant, confirm the operative provision."
