    "title": "Health and safety — breaches",
    "sectionId": "para-1452",
    "filename": "Rockwater Group Employee Handbook (April 2026).docx",
    "context": "[para-1448] If employees are attending the premises of a third party or service user, they are required to familiarise themselves with the applicable policies and procedures.\n\n[para-1450] Employees should ensure they handle any hazardous materials with care.\n\n[para-1452] Breaching any rules surrounding health and safety may lead to disciplinary action. A breach may be considered gross misconduct which can result in summary termination of employment.\n\n[para-1454] Smoking\n\n[para-1455] In accordance with the Health Act 2006, the Organisation does not permit smoking in the workplace, either on Organisation premises or in Organisation cars. The Organisation promotes a working environment which is smoke-free, pleasant and healthy. This prohibition extends to the use of e-cigarettes or similar devices.",
    "note": "Original DOCX paragraph anchors count blank paragraphs and are not page numbers. This is documentary wording, not a finding about the incident. The supplied handbook contains template placeholders elsewhere; where relevant, confirm the operative provision."
