    "context": "[PDF page 1; public edition with explicit redactions]\n\nRockwater Hove\nAssistant Manager Offer Letter\nDear [EMPLOYEE NAME REDACTED],\nWe’re delighted to extend this offer of employment for the position of Assistant Manager with Rockwater Hove .\nPlease review this summary of terms and conditions for your anticipated employment with us. If you accept this\noffer, your start date will be April 22, 2026 and you would report to [MANAGER NAME REDACTED].\nPlease find below the summary of the terms and conditions of your employment, should you accept this offer\nletter:\nPosition\nYour title will be Assistant Manager, and you will report to the Restaurant Manager. This is a full time position\nrequiring an average of 40 on a rota basis. You are required to work at [WORKPLACE ADDRESS REDACTED]. However, you may from time to time be required to work in other locations or to\ntransfer permanently to another business unit in the area. You are expected to comply with any reasonable\nrequest.\nCompensation and Benefits\nRockwater Hove will pay you a starting salary at the rate of [PAY REDACTED] per hour, payable in accordance with the\nCompany’s standard payroll schedule, beginning April 22, 2026 .\nAs a regular employee of the Company, you will be eligible for the following non contractual company benefits\n25% Discount on food for you and up to three guests when you dine with us\nA complimentary staff meal during your shift when you are on duty\nComplimentary, tea, coffee and soft drinks when you are working on shift\nAt the discretion of the duty manager a glass of house wine or beer directly after the end of your working\nshift\nWellbeing Services Programme, including a 24/7 emergency telephone support.\nYou will also receive tronc which is worked out on a point based system. Levels of tronc may fluctuate due to\nthe changing levels of service charge coming into the business.\nHolidays\nThe holiday year runs from 1st March to 28 February (29 in a leap year). If your employment starts or finishes\npart way through the holiday year, your holiday entitlement during that year shall be calculated on a pro-rata\nbasis. In each annual holiday year, you are entitled to take 28 days paid leave, including the eight statutory\nholidays (or the pro-rata equivalent if you work part-time), where one day equals one fifth of your normal\nworking week. Holiday accrues at 1/52 of your annual entitlement for each completed week of service.\nProbationary Period\nThe first three months of your employment are covered by a probationary period, when the disciplinary\nprocedures may not apply. Your contract of employment may be ended at any time during this period if you are\nfailing to achieve the necessary standards of performance and/or conduct for the successful achievement of\nyour role.\nYou may indicate your agreement with these terms and accept this offer by signing and dating this agreement\non or before Offer Expires On. Upon your acceptance of this employment offer, Company Name will provide\nyou with the necessary paperwork and instructions for your onboarding.",
